Build fixes for native IRIX hosts and legacy IRIX headers

Changes needed to build the compiler suite on IRIX itself and against
IRIX headers: IRIX's missing snprintf in libbacktrace, libcody,
libiberty and zlib; <sys/types.h> includes before socket and mmap users;
the pid_t pex_unix_wait signature; PRI*64 fallbacks in hwint.h and
sreal.cc; disabling libcody networking; and the gcc/cp mapper client's
socket headers.

None of these are needed for an x86-host cross build (the sgi/__sgi
paths are inactive), but they are part of the pdaxrom IRIX layer and
keep the series a complete port.

Provenance: pdaxrom/irix-gcc tag 1.2 (2aa3421b), gcc-15.2.0-irix.diff.

